{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UwWoCSGqeynRyqy2xj8jzQ","type":"tool_result","content":"package setupcmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/cli\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/effects\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels/labelsync\"\n)\n\n// Command is the handler behind `ard setup`. The config is loaded and\n// validated before any GitHub client exists.\nfunc Command(ctx context.Context, e *cli.Env, o cli.SetupOpts) error {\n\troot, err := config.RepoRoot(e.ConfigPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tres, err := config.Load(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\twant, err := labels.Desired(labels.SpecFrom(res))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\trepo, err := labelsync.ResolveRepo(ctx, e, root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif o.CreateGHApp {\n\t\tif err := CreateApp(ctx, e, repo, CreateAppOpts{Name: o.AppName, KeyPath: o.KeyFile, Force: o.Force}); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif e.DryRun {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tauth, err := github.AuthFromEnv(os.Getenv, os.ReadFile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tdry := e.DryRun && !o.Check\n\tfx, rd, err := effects.Open(ctx, effects.Options{\n\t\tDryRun: dry,\n\t\tGitHub: github.Config{Repo: repo, Auth: auth, Log: e.Log},\n\t\tLog:    e.Log,\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\td := Deps{\n\t\tReader:      rd,\n\t\tPolicy:      rd,\n\t\tRepo:        repo,\n\t\tWriter:      fx,\n\t\tDesired:     want,\n\t\tPermissions: func(ctx context.Context) Row { return CheckPermissions(ctx, rd, repo) },\n\t\tLocalVsMain: func(ctx context.Context) (string, error) { return LocalVsMain(ctx, root) },\n\t\tDryRun:      dry,\n\t\tLog:         e.Log,\n\t}\n\treturn execute(ctx, e, d, o)\n}\n\n// execute runs setup with the given dependencies and maps the report to\n// the command's outcome: exit 2 on drift under --check, an error when\n// manual steps are needed.\nfunc execute(ctx context.Context, e *cli.Env, d Deps, o cli.SetupOpts) error {\n\trep, err := Run(ctx, d, Opts{Check: o.Check}, e.Stdout)\n\tPrint(e.Stdout, rep, d.DryRun)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif o.Check && rep.HasDrift() {\n\t\treturn &cli.ExitError{Code: 2, Err: errors.New(\"setup: drift\")}\n\t}\n\tif !rep.Green() {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"setup: manual steps needed\")\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// LocalVsMain returns a warning when ./.ard/ in the worktree differs from\n// origin/main, which is what ard serve reads. It never fails the run.\nfunc LocalVsMain(ctx context.Context, root string) (string, error) {\n\tg := gitx.New(\"\")\n\tif _, err := g.RevParse(ctx, root, \"origin/main\"); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"origin/main not found; cannot compare ./.ard/ with what ard serve reads\", nil\n\t}\n\tch, err := g.ChangedSince(ctx, root, root, \"origin/main\", \".ard/\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tif len(ch) > 0 {\n\t\treturn \"./.ard/ differs from origin/main (ard serve reads origin/main)\", nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", nil\n}\n\n// CheckPermissions is the permission check shared by `ard setup` and\n// `ard init`. Until the full check (#302) lands it only verifies that the\n// repository is readable with the configured credentials.\nfunc CheckPermissions(ctx context.Context, r labelsync.Reader, repo github.Repo) Row {\n\tif _, err := r.ListLabels(ctx); err != nil {\n\t\treturn Row{Status: StatusManual, Detail: \"check ARD_GITHUB_* credentials and that the App is installed on \" + repo.String() + \" with the permissions in AppPermissions (never \" + strings.Join(ForbiddenPermissions, \", \") + \")\"}\n\t}\n\treturn Row{Status: StatusOK, Detail: \"repository reachable\"}\n}\npackage setupcmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"errors\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels/labelsync\"\n)\n\n// Opts are the flags of `ard setup`.\ntype Opts struct{ Check bool }\n\n// PolicyReader is the read-only GitHub surface of the policy checks.\ntype PolicyReader interface {\n\tIdentity(ctx context.Context) (github.Identity, error)\n\tListRulesets(ctx context.Context) ([]github.Ruleset, error)\n\tGetMergeSettings(ctx context.Context) (github.MergeSettings, error)\n\tGetApp(ctx context.Context, slug string) (github.AppInfo, error)\n\tGetVariable(ctx context.Context, name string) (string, bool, error)\n}\n\n// Deps is what Run needs from the outside world.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tReader      labelsync.Reader\n\tWriter      labelsync.Writer // the effect layer: a dry-run writer writes nothing\n\tDesired     []labels.Label\n\tPermissions func(ctx context.Context) Row\n\tLocalVsMain func(ctx context.Context) (warning string, err error)\n\t// Policy, when set, enables the ruleset, App permission and merge\n\t// setting checks for Repo. They only read.\n\tPolicy PolicyReader\n\tRepo   github.Repo\n\tDryRun bool\n\tLog    *slog.Logger\n}\n\nconst (\n\tpermName  = \"permissions\"\n\tlabelName = \"labels\"\n\n\trulesetName = \"ruleset\"\n\tappPermName = \"app-permissions\"\n\tmergeName   = \"merge-settings\"\n)\n\n// Run executes the checks, then applies when the permission row is ok and\n// Check is not set. The returned report holds the final rows.\nfunc Run(ctx context.Context, d Deps, o Opts, out io.Writer) (Report, error) {\n\tif d.LocalVsMain != nil {\n\t\tw, err := d.LocalVsMain(ctx)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tw = \"could not compare ./.ard/ with origin/main\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tif w != \"\" {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"warning: %s\\n\", w)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tperm := Row{Name: permName, Status: StatusOK}\n\tif d.Permissions != nil {\n\t\tperm = d.Permissions(ctx)\n\t\tperm.Name = permName\n\t}\n\trep := Report{Rows: []Row{perm}}\n\tif perm.Status != StatusOK {\n\t\t// Nothing else can be read reliably without access.\n\t\treturn rep, nil\n\t}\n\tif d.Policy != nil {\n\t\trows, err := policyRows(ctx, d)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn rep, err\n\t\t}\n\t\trep.Rows = append(rep.Rows, rows...)\n\t}\n\t// Apply only when every check is green; label drift alone is fixable.\n\tblocked := !rep.Green()\n\thave, err := d.Reader.ListLabels(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn rep, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: list labels: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tplan := labelsync.Diff(have, d.Desired)\n\trow := Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusOK}\n\tif n, m := len(plan.Create), len(plan.Update); n+m > 0 {\n\t\trow.Status = StatusDrift\n\t\trow.Detail = fmt.Sprintf(\"%d to create, %d to update\", n, m)\n\t}\n\tif len(plan.Stale) > 0 {\n\t\tsep := \"\"\n\t\tif row.Detail != \"\" {\n\t\t\tsep = \"; \"\n\t\t}\n\t\trow.Detail += sep + \"stale (not deleted): \" + strings.Join(plan.Stale, \", \")\n\t}\n\trep.Rows = append(rep.Rows, row)\n\tif o.Check || blocked || row.Status != StatusDrift {\n\t\treturn rep, nil\n\t}\n\n\tsr, err := labelsync.Sync(ctx, d.Reader, d.Writer, d.Desired, d.Log)\n\tif err != nil && sr.Failed == nil {\n\t\treturn rep, err\n\t}\n\trow = Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusChanged}\n\tswitch {\n\tcase len(sr.Failed) > 0:\n\t\tvar names []string\n\t\tfor n := range sr.Failed {\n\t\t\tnames = append(names, n)\n\t\t}\n\t\tsort.Strings(names)\n\t\trow = Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusManual, Detail: \"create or update these labels by hand: \" + strings.Join(names, \", \")}\n\tcase d.DryRun:\n\t\trow.Detail = fmt.Sprintf(\"would create %d, would update %d\", len(sr.Create), len(sr.Update))\n\tdefault:\n\t\trow.Detail = fmt.Sprintf(\"created %d, updated %d\", len(sr.Create), len(sr.Update))\n\t}\n\trep.Rows[len(rep.Rows)-1] = row\n\treturn rep, err\n}\n\n// policyRows runs the read-only policy checks. A forbidden or unknown-App\n// read gives a manual row with the exact command to look it up by hand.\nfunc policyRows(ctx context.Context, d Deps) ([]Row, error) {\n\trepo := d.Repo\n\tmanual := func(name, detail string) Row { return Row{Name: name, Status: StatusManual, Detail: detail} }\n\tsoft := func(err error) bool { return errors.Is(err, github.ErrForbidden) || errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) }\n\n\tid, err := d.Policy.Identity(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: identity: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tslug := strings.TrimSuffix(id.Login, \"[bot]\")\n\tvar rows []Row\n\n\tapp, appErr := d.Policy.GetApp(ctx, slug)\n\tif appErr != nil && !soft(appErr) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: get app: %w\", appErr)\n\t}\n\tappCmd := \"gh api apps/\" + slug\n\trs, rsErr := d.Policy.ListRulesets(ctx)\n\tswitch {\n\tcase rsErr != nil && !soft(rsErr):\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: list rulesets: %w\", rsErr)\n\tcase rsErr != nil:\n\t\trows = append(rows, manual(rulesetName, \"admin read is needed; check \"+rulesURL(repo)+\" or run: gh api repos/\"+repo.String()+\"/rulesets\"))\n\tcase appErr != nil:\n\t\trows = append(rows, manual(rulesetName, \"cannot resolve the App; run: \"+appCmd))\n\tdefault:\n\t\trows = append(rows, checkRuleset(repo, rs, app))\n\t}\n\tif appErr != nil {\n\t\trows = append(rows, manual(appPermName, \"cannot read the App; run: \"+appCmd+\" and check the permissions at \"+installURL(repo)))\n\t} else {\n\t\trows = append(rows, checkAppPerms(repo, app))\n\t}\n\n\tms, err := d.Policy.GetMergeSettings(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif !soft(err) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: merge settings: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn append(rows, manual(mergeName, \"cannot read merge settings; run: gh api repos/\"+repo.String())), nil\n\t}\n\tv, found, err := d.Policy.GetVariable(ctx, policyVersioning)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif !soft(err) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: read %s: %w\", policyVersioning, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn append(rows, manual(mergeName, fmt.Sprintf(\"cannot read the %s variable; run: gh variable get %s -R %s\", policyVersioning, policyVersioning, repo))), nil\n\t}\n\treturn append(rows, checkMerge(repo, ms, found && versioningOn(v))), nil\n}\n# Detective control for the main-lane committer (docs/proposal.md, \"The .ard/\n# contract\"). The bot bypasses branch protection on main, so this audits the\n# first-parent history of main and fails when a commit made by the bot changes\n# anything except regular files under a single .ard/<issue#>/ directory.\n#\n# The bot login and the optional baseline come from repository variables, which\n# the GitHub App cannot write. The App also lacks the `workflows` permission,\n# so it cannot edit this file. Both are why the logic is inline bash here and\n# not Go. internal/botcheck extracts the script below and tests it.\nname: ard bot commits\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  # Main-lane bot pushes carry [skip ci], which suppresses the push trigger, so\n  # a schedule is what catches a stretch of history made only of bot commits.\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '17 * * * *'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    steps:\nmake build   # bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet + gofmt check\nmake fmt     # gofmt -w\n```\n\nRun `make lint test` before every commit.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Tests: table-driven, no network. Use the GitHub fake for unit tests; real-API tests go behind the `integration` build tag.\n- Errors: wrap with context (`fmt.Errorf(\"claim issue %d: %w\", n, err)`); never swallow.\n- Logging: structured (`log/slog`), one event per claim, close-out and failure.\n- Keep packages small and interfaces at the consumer.\n\n## Workflow\n\n- Work is tracked in GitHub issues with `phase:N`, `area:*` and `type:*` labels and a phase milestone. Pick from the lowest open phase.\n- Branch per issue: `<issue#>-<short-slug>`. Open a PR that says `Closes #<issue>`. Do not push to `main` directly.\n- Keep PRs to one issue. Note follow-ups as new issues rather than widening the PR.\n- Decision issues (`type:decision`) record the choice in a comment, then update the proposal and close.\n- No AI attribution in commits or PRs: no `Co-Authored-By: Claude …` trailers, and no \"Generated with Claude Code\" lines in PR descriptions or comments.\n44:func IsSynthetic(n int) bool { return n < 0 }\n54:type Effects interface {\n70:func isNothing(err error) bool { return errors.Is(err, ErrNothingToCommit) }\n./.ard-input/348/comments.md:10:This extends `ard setup` in two ways. It sets the repository variable for the bot login, taken from the App identity, through a new effect-layer call. It also checks the repository's bot-commits workflow against a copy embedded in ard and adds a flag that prints that copy. Both dependencies (the first `ard setup` command in `internal/setupcmd` and the GitHub connectivity and token work) are already in this checkout, so the work can start now. The engineer triage role is the only planner, so it plans the whole change.\n./.ard-input/348/issue.md:9:ard init and setup, part F: ARD_BOT_LOGIN variable and the bot-commits workflow\n./.ard-input/348/issue.md:13:Apply `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (derived from the App's identity, `<slug>[bot]`, never from config; never overwrite a different existing value without confirmation) through a new `SetRepoVariable` on the effect layer, with the operator's token (`gh auth token` or a PAT, in memory only; see #302). Check `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` on `origin/main` against a copy embedded in ard; `ard setup --print-workflow` prints it for a human to commit; setup never commits.\n./deploy/test-repo.sh:32:  git diff --quiet \"$base\" -- .github/workflows/ci.yml .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\n./internal/botcheck/doc.go:2:// inline script in step \"check\" of .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml; the tests\n./internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go:28:const workflowPath = \"../../.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\"\n./internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go:330:\t\t}, 2, []string{\"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\"}},\n./internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go:514:\t\t\tfor k, v := range map[string]string{\"BOT_LOGIN\": \"vars.ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"SINCE\": \"vars.ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE\"} {\n./internal/initcmd/body.go:64:\tb.WriteString(\"1. Copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from the ard repository into this repository.\\n\")\n./internal/initcmd/body.go:65:\tb.WriteString(\"2. Set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login.\\n\")\n./internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:210:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/`\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n./docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md:49:  here): copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from this repository, then set\n./docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md:50:  the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login.\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:18:- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:27:`version.yml`'s `tag` job mints a short-lived token from this App (`actions/create-github-app-token`) to push tags and create releases. It is a separate App from ard's so that ard's own token can never create a tag; the job refuses to run if the two are the same (it compares the App's slug with `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`).\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:46:   Check that `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` is also set to ard's own App login (`gh variable list -R albertcbrown/ard`).\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:61:A tag ruleset keeps tags immutable and lets only the release App create them. `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`'s App, workflows using `GITHUB_TOKEN` and people without bypass cannot create, move or delete a `v*` tag.\n./docs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:144:3. **Bot-commit audit.** Set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to\n./docs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:145:   `ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot]`; without it `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml`\n./docs/site/getting-started.md:61:Also audit the bot's commits. Set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login, and add a workflow that fails when a bot commit changes anything outside a single `.ard/<issue#>/` directory. The example is [.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/main/.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml). The App cannot write workflows, so you add this one yourself.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7aad3249-fab4-4007-998f-661508877ca3","uuid":"1b30c750-f7de-4aa0-8f54-69ca80466763","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:02:07.677Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"package setupcmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/cli\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/effects\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels/labelsync\"\n)\n\n// Command is the handler behind `ard setup`. The config is loaded and\n// validated before any GitHub client exists.\nfunc Command(ctx context.Context, e *cli.Env, o cli.SetupOpts) error {\n\troot, err := config.RepoRoot(e.ConfigPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tres, err := config.Load(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\twant, err := labels.Desired(labels.SpecFrom(res))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\trepo, err := labelsync.ResolveRepo(ctx, e, root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif o.CreateGHApp {\n\t\tif err := CreateApp(ctx, e, repo, CreateAppOpts{Name: o.AppName, KeyPath: o.KeyFile, Force: o.Force}); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif e.DryRun {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tauth, err := github.AuthFromEnv(os.Getenv, os.ReadFile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tdry := e.DryRun && !o.Check\n\tfx, rd, err := effects.Open(ctx, effects.Options{\n\t\tDryRun: dry,\n\t\tGitHub: github.Config{Repo: repo, Auth: auth, Log: e.Log},\n\t\tLog:    e.Log,\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"setup: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\td := Deps{\n\t\tReader:      rd,\n\t\tPolicy:      rd,\n\t\tRepo:        repo,\n\t\tWriter:      fx,\n\t\tDesired:     want,\n\t\tPermissions: func(ctx context.Context) Row { return CheckPermissions(ctx, rd, repo) },\n\t\tLocalVsMain: func(ctx context.Context) (string, error) { return LocalVsMain(ctx, root) },\n\t\tDryRun:      dry,\n\t\tLog:         e.Log,\n\t}\n\treturn execute(ctx, e, d, o)\n}\n\n// execute runs setup with the given dependencies and maps the report to\n// the command's outcome: exit 2 on drift under --check, an error when\n// manual steps are needed.\nfunc execute(ctx context.Context, e *cli.Env, d Deps, o cli.SetupOpts) error {\n\trep, err := Run(ctx, d, Opts{Check: o.Check}, e.Stdout)\n\tPrint(e.Stdout, rep, d.DryRun)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif o.Check && rep.HasDrift() {\n\t\treturn &cli.ExitError{Code: 2, Err: errors.New(\"setup: drift\")}\n\t}\n\tif !rep.Green() {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"setup: manual steps needed\")\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// LocalVsMain returns a warning when ./.ard/ in the worktree differs from\n// origin/main, which is what ard serve reads. It never fails the run.\nfunc LocalVsMain(ctx context.Context, root string) (string, error) {\n\tg := gitx.New(\"\")\n\tif _, err := g.RevParse(ctx, root, \"origin/main\"); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"origin/main not found; cannot compare ./.ard/ with what ard serve reads\", nil\n\t}\n\tch, err := g.ChangedSince(ctx, root, root, \"origin/main\", \".ard/\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tif len(ch) > 0 {\n\t\treturn \"./.ard/ differs from origin/main (ard serve reads origin/main)\", nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", nil\n}\n\n// CheckPermissions is the permission check shared by `ard setup` and\n// `ard init`. Until the full check (#302) lands it only verifies that the\n// repository is readable with the configured credentials.\nfunc CheckPermissions(ctx context.Context, r labelsync.Reader, repo github.Repo) Row {\n\tif _, err := r.ListLabels(ctx); err != nil {\n\t\treturn Row{Status: StatusManual, Detail: \"check ARD_GITHUB_* credentials and that the App is installed on \" + repo.String() + \" with the permissions in AppPermissions (never \" + strings.Join(ForbiddenPermissions, \", \") + \")\"}\n\t}\n\treturn Row{Status: StatusOK, Detail: \"repository reachable\"}\n}\npackage setupcmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"errors\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels/labelsync\"\n)\n\n// Opts are the flags of `ard setup`.\ntype Opts struct{ Check bool }\n\n// PolicyReader is the read-only GitHub surface of the policy checks.\ntype PolicyReader interface {\n\tIdentity(ctx context.Context) (github.Identity, error)\n\tListRulesets(ctx context.Context) ([]github.Ruleset, error)\n\tGetMergeSettings(ctx context.Context) (github.MergeSettings, error)\n\tGetApp(ctx context.Context, slug string) (github.AppInfo, error)\n\tGetVariable(ctx context.Context, name string) (string, bool, error)\n}\n\n// Deps is what Run needs from the outside world.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tReader      labelsync.Reader\n\tWriter      labelsync.Writer // the effect layer: a dry-run writer writes nothing\n\tDesired     []labels.Label\n\tPermissions func(ctx context.Context) Row\n\tLocalVsMain func(ctx context.Context) (warning string, err error)\n\t// Policy, when set, enables the ruleset, App permission and merge\n\t// setting checks for Repo. They only read.\n\tPolicy PolicyReader\n\tRepo   github.Repo\n\tDryRun bool\n\tLog    *slog.Logger\n}\n\nconst (\n\tpermName  = \"permissions\"\n\tlabelName = \"labels\"\n\n\trulesetName = \"ruleset\"\n\tappPermName = \"app-permissions\"\n\tmergeName   = \"merge-settings\"\n)\n\n// Run executes the checks, then applies when the permission row is ok and\n// Check is not set. The returned report holds the final rows.\nfunc Run(ctx context.Context, d Deps, o Opts, out io.Writer) (Report, error) {\n\tif d.LocalVsMain != nil {\n\t\tw, err := d.LocalVsMain(ctx)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tw = \"could not compare ./.ard/ with origin/main\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tif w != \"\" {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"warning: %s\\n\", w)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tperm := Row{Name: permName, Status: StatusOK}\n\tif d.Permissions != nil {\n\t\tperm = d.Permissions(ctx)\n\t\tperm.Name = permName\n\t}\n\trep := Report{Rows: []Row{perm}}\n\tif perm.Status != StatusOK {\n\t\t// Nothing else can be read reliably without access.\n\t\treturn rep, nil\n\t}\n\tif d.Policy != nil {\n\t\trows, err := policyRows(ctx, d)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn rep, err\n\t\t}\n\t\trep.Rows = append(rep.Rows, rows...)\n\t}\n\t// Apply only when every check is green; label drift alone is fixable.\n\tblocked := !rep.Green()\n\thave, err := d.Reader.ListLabels(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn rep, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: list labels: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tplan := labelsync.Diff(have, d.Desired)\n\trow := Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusOK}\n\tif n, m := len(plan.Create), len(plan.Update); n+m > 0 {\n\t\trow.Status = StatusDrift\n\t\trow.Detail = fmt.Sprintf(\"%d to create, %d to update\", n, m)\n\t}\n\tif len(plan.Stale) > 0 {\n\t\tsep := \"\"\n\t\tif row.Detail != \"\" {\n\t\t\tsep = \"; \"\n\t\t}\n\t\trow.Detail += sep + \"stale (not deleted): \" + strings.Join(plan.Stale, \", \")\n\t}\n\trep.Rows = append(rep.Rows, row)\n\tif o.Check || blocked || row.Status != StatusDrift {\n\t\treturn rep, nil\n\t}\n\n\tsr, err := labelsync.Sync(ctx, d.Reader, d.Writer, d.Desired, d.Log)\n\tif err != nil && sr.Failed == nil {\n\t\treturn rep, err\n\t}\n\trow = Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusChanged}\n\tswitch {\n\tcase len(sr.Failed) > 0:\n\t\tvar names []string\n\t\tfor n := range sr.Failed {\n\t\t\tnames = append(names, n)\n\t\t}\n\t\tsort.Strings(names)\n\t\trow = Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusManual, Detail: \"create or update these labels by hand: \" + strings.Join(names, \", \")}\n\tcase d.DryRun:\n\t\trow.Detail = fmt.Sprintf(\"would create %d, would update %d\", len(sr.Create), len(sr.Update))\n\tdefault:\n\t\trow.Detail = fmt.Sprintf(\"created %d, updated %d\", len(sr.Create), len(sr.Update))\n\t}\n\trep.Rows[len(rep.Rows)-1] = row\n\treturn rep, err\n}\n\n// policyRows runs the read-only policy checks. A forbidden or unknown-App\n// read gives a manual row with the exact command to look it up by hand.\nfunc policyRows(ctx context.Context, d Deps) ([]Row, error) {\n\trepo := d.Repo\n\tmanual := func(name, detail string) Row { return Row{Name: name, Status: StatusManual, Detail: detail} }\n\tsoft := func(err error) bool { return errors.Is(err, github.ErrForbidden) || errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) }\n\n\tid, err := d.Policy.Identity(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: identity: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tslug := strings.TrimSuffix(id.Login, \"[bot]\")\n\tvar rows []Row\n\n\tapp, appErr := d.Policy.GetApp(ctx, slug)\n\tif appErr != nil && !soft(appErr) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: get app: %w\", appErr)\n\t}\n\tappCmd := \"gh api apps/\" + slug\n\trs, rsErr := d.Policy.ListRulesets(ctx)\n\tswitch {\n\tcase rsErr != nil && !soft(rsErr):\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: list rulesets: %w\", rsErr)\n\tcase rsErr != nil:\n\t\trows = append(rows, manual(rulesetName, \"admin read is needed; check \"+rulesURL(repo)+\" or run: gh api repos/\"+repo.String()+\"/rulesets\"))\n\tcase appErr != nil:\n\t\trows = append(rows, manual(rulesetName, \"cannot resolve the App; run: \"+appCmd))\n\tdefault:\n\t\trows = append(rows, checkRuleset(repo, rs, app))\n\t}\n\tif appErr != nil {\n\t\trows = append(rows, manual(appPermName, \"cannot read the App; run: \"+appCmd+\" and check the permissions at \"+installURL(repo)))\n\t} else {\n\t\trows = append(rows, checkAppPerms(repo, app))\n\t}\n\n\tms, err := d.Policy.GetMergeSettings(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif !soft(err) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: merge settings: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn append(rows, manual(mergeName, \"cannot read merge settings; run: gh api repos/\"+repo.String())), nil\n\t}\n\tv, found, err := d.Policy.GetVariable(ctx, policyVersioning)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif !soft(err) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"setup: read %s: %w\", policyVersioning, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn append(rows, manual(mergeName, fmt.Sprintf(\"cannot read the %s variable; run: gh variable get %s -R %s\", policyVersioning, policyVersioning, repo))), nil\n\t}\n\treturn append(rows, checkMerge(repo, ms, found && versioningOn(v))), nil\n}\n# Detective control for the main-lane committer (docs/proposal.md, \"The .ard/\n# contract\"). The bot bypasses branch protection on main, so this audits the\n# first-parent history of main and fails when a commit made by the bot changes\n# anything except regular files under a single .ard/<issue#>/ directory.\n#\n# The bot login and the optional baseline come from repository variables, which\n# the GitHub App cannot write. The App also lacks the `workflows` permission,\n# so it cannot edit this file. Both are why the logic is inline bash here and\n# not Go. internal/botcheck extracts the script below and tests it.\nname: ard bot commits\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  # Main-lane bot pushes carry [skip ci], which suppresses the push trigger, so\n  # a schedule is what catches a stretch of history made only of bot commits.\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '17 * * * *'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    steps:\nmake build   # bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet + gofmt check\nmake fmt     # gofmt -w\n```\n\nRun `make lint test` before every commit.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Tests: table-driven, no network. Use the GitHub fake for unit tests; real-API tests go behind the `integration` build tag.\n- Errors: wrap with context (`fmt.Errorf(\"claim issue %d: %w\", n, err)`); never swallow.\n- Logging: structured (`log/slog`), one event per claim, close-out and failure.\n- Keep packages small and interfaces at the consumer.\n\n## Workflow\n\n- Work is tracked in GitHub issues with `phase:N`, `area:*` and `type:*` labels and a phase milestone. Pick from the lowest open phase.\n- Branch per issue: `<issue#>-<short-slug>`. Open a PR that says `Closes #<issue>`. Do not push to `main` directly.\n- Keep PRs to one issue. Note follow-ups as new issues rather than widening the PR.\n- Decision issues (`type:decision`) record the choice in a comment, then update the proposal and close.\n- No AI attribution in commits or PRs: no `Co-Authored-By: Claude …` trailers, and no \"Generated with Claude Code\" lines in PR descriptions or comments.\n44:func IsSynthetic(n int) bool { return n < 0 }\n54:type Effects interface {\n70:func isNothing(err error) bool { return errors.Is(err, ErrNothingToCommit) }\n./.ard-input/348/comments.md:10:This extends `ard setup` in two ways. It sets the repository variable for the bot login, taken from the App identity, through a new effect-layer call. It also checks the repository's bot-commits workflow against a copy embedded in ard and adds a flag that prints that copy. Both dependencies (the first `ard setup` command in `internal/setupcmd` and the GitHub connectivity and token work) are already in this checkout, so the work can start now. The engineer triage role is the only planner, so it plans the whole change.\n./.ard-input/348/issue.md:9:ard init and setup, part F: ARD_BOT_LOGIN variable and the bot-commits workflow\n./.ard-input/348/issue.md:13:Apply `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (derived from the App's identity, `<slug>[bot]`, never from config; never overwrite a different existing value without confirmation) through a new `SetRepoVariable` on the effect layer, with the operator's token (`gh auth token` or a PAT, in memory only; see #302). Check `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` on `origin/main` against a copy embedded in ard; `ard setup --print-workflow` prints it for a human to commit; setup never commits.\n./deploy/test-repo.sh:32:  git diff --quiet \"$base\" -- .github/workflows/ci.yml .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\n./internal/botcheck/doc.go:2:// inline script in step \"check\" of .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml; the tests\n./internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go:28:const workflowPath = \"../../.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\"\n./internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go:330:\t\t}, 2, []string{\"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\"}},\n./internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go:514:\t\t\tfor k, v := range map[string]string{\"BOT_LOGIN\": \"vars.ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"SINCE\": \"vars.ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE\"} {\n./internal/initcmd/body.go:64:\tb.WriteString(\"1. Copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from the ard repository into this repository.\\n\")\n./internal/initcmd/body.go:65:\tb.WriteString(\"2. Set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login.\\n\")\n./internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:210:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/`\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n./docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md:49:  here): copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from this repository, then set\n./docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md:50:  the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login.\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:18:- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:27:`version.yml`'s `tag` job mints a short-lived token from this App (`actions/create-github-app-token`) to push tags and create releases. It is a separate App from ard's so that ard's own token can never create a tag; the job refuses to run if the two are the same (it compares the App's slug with `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`).\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:46:   Check that `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` is also set to ard's own App login (`gh variable list -R albertcbrown/ard`).\n./docs/runbooks/release.md:61:A tag ruleset keeps tags immutable and lets only the release App create them. `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`'s App, workflows using `GITHUB_TOKEN` and people without bypass cannot create, move or delete a `v*` tag.\n./docs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:144:3. **Bot-commit audit.** Set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to\n./docs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:145:   `ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot]`; without it `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml`\n./docs/site/getting-started.md:61:Also audit the bot's commits. Set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` to the App's `<slug>[bot]` login, and add a workflow that fails when a bot commit changes anything outside a single `.ard/<issue#>/` directory. The example is [.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/main/.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml). The App cannot write workflows, so you add this one yourself.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UwWoCSGqeynRyqy2xj8jzQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
